        "body":  "\u003e Thank you for raising this issue. I have created a new release v1.0.3 detailed in PR [#3](https://github.com/dfl-rlab/erc_sim_2026/pull/3), which resolves the book spine width issue and adds range limits to the grippers so you can now pick them up fine without getting stuck at 0.07. We set the rule of not modifying the robot model so that there are no discrepancies between the urdf file in simulation and the physical robot. We will get back to you soon regarding the effort interface point\n\nThank you for the reply. We pulled v1.0.3 and re-tested.\n\nThe book resize and the friction increase both work as intended, and we found and fixed a regression on our own side from the new dimensions.\n\nOne correction though: the books still can\u0027t be picked up. We re-ran the free-space isolation test book placed between the open jaws within 1 mm, spine square across them and the fingers close through it to the free-air closed position (q = 0, tip separation 0.02795 m) while reporting 3038 contact events involving the book. So the grasp is still blocked pending the effort interface. No rush on that, just flagging that this release didn\u0027t unblock it.\n\nTwo smaller things from the release you may want to know:\n\n1. **/gripper_*_controller/follow_joint_trajectory** no longer exists the clamp node is a topic relay only. Your README documents the action interface as a supported path, so this may catch out teams using it.\n\n2. The 0.07 latch is masked rather than fixed: the clamp rejects 0.07, but the latch is still live on the **_raw** topic.",
        "author_association":  "NONE",
        "pin":  null,
