        "created_at":  "2026-08-27T19:41:33Z",
        "updated_at":  "2026-08-27T19:41:33Z",
        "body":  "On the effort-interface question — I think the answer is that adding one would\nnot have fixed it, and the reason is in the `gz_ros2_control` copy vendored in\nthis repo rather than in the robot model.\n\n## Two things in `src/gz_ros2_control/gz_ros2_control/src/gz_system.cpp`\n\n**1. The mimic EFFORT interface is registered under the wrong predicate**\n(around line 377):\n\n```cpp\nbool vel = interface_info.name == \"velocity\";\nif (vel) {mimic_joint.interfaces_to_mimic.push_back(hardware_interface::HW_IF_VELOCITY);}\nbool eff = interface_info.name == \"effort\";\nif (vel) {mimic_joint.interfaces_to_mimic.push_back(hardware_interface::HW_IF_EFFORT);}\n```\n\n`eff` is computed and never used — the effort push is gated on `vel`. So a mimic\njoint declaring only an effort interface registers **nothing**. This is not\nspecific to your fork; it is identical on upstream `ros-controls/gz_ros2_control`\n`humble`, which is the branch pinned here. I have reported it there\n(ros-controls/gz_ros2_control#951) so the fix lands for everyone rather than\nonly in this repo.\n\n**2. The position-mimic path is a pure kinematic drive.** Further down the same\nfile, the mimic position branch computes\n\n```cpp\nvelocity_sp = -position_error * update_rate;   // -\u003e sim::components::JointVelocityCmd\n```\n\nNo force or effort limit enters that loop. The fingertips\u0027 `effort=\"0.1\"` is\nnever consulted, and the joint is driven to a position regardless of what it is\npressing against.\n\nThat predicts both reported observations exactly: the fingers close **through**\nthe book while logging thousands of contact events, and raising\n`position_proportional_gain` by a large factor only raises commanded joint\nvelocity rather than contact force — which is what @WinnieThepo observed.\n\n## The force budget, so the decision does not rest on intuition\n\nFrom the shipped assets — book mass 0.3 kg, `\u003cmu\u003e5.0\u003c/mu\u003e`,\n`gripper_*_finger_joint` prismatic `effort=\"10.0\"`, fingertips revolute\n`effort=\"0.1\"` N·m — the normal force needed per pad to hold the book against\ngravity is\n\n```\nF = m g / (2 mu) = (0.3 x 9.81) / (2 x 5.0) = 0.294 N        (1.47 N if the pad\u0027s mu is 1.0)\n```\n\nagainst a 10 N prismatic limit and roughly 2-3 N of fingertip capacity at a\n0.03-0.05 m pad lever. **Force capacity was never the binding constraint** —\nwhich is the useful part for the decision in front of you: an effort command\ninterface alone will not fix this while the fingertips remain kinematically\ndriven mimic joints. The two changes are independent and only the second one is\nload-bearing.\n\nI have not run your stack, so the force numbers are from the declared asset\nvalues rather than from a rollout — worth sanity-checking against a real grasp\nonce the mimic path is settled. The two code readings above are directly\ncheckable in this repository.\n\n(Noting @The-Real-Thisas reported a working version on 2026-08-26 — if that\nalready routes around the mimic path then this is confirmation rather than news,\nand the upstream report is the part that still matters.)\n",
        "author_association":  "NONE",
        "pin":  null,
