        "created_at":  "2026-09-04T11:29:07Z",
        "updated_at":  "2026-09-04T11:29:07Z",
        "body":  "I\u0027ve made some additions to the issue_gripper_effort branch (commit https://github.com/dfl-rlab/erc_sim_2026/commit/8b5f26187d17172aed8877ec4b21d8ecd239a848) in regards to this issue, can you please try it and let us know if you are able to lift the books fine? we tested it on our end in the video attached. \n\nThe physical TIAGo Pro gripper hardware only includes position as a command interface, and position, velocity, and effort as state interfaces (check config file here https://github.com/pal-robotics/pal_pro_gripper/tree/humble-devel). We want to avoid making changes to the URDF that would deviate from the physical hardware such as adding effort as a command interface, as was proposed as a solution above. As a possible workaround is using the position controller and the effort interface feedback from the gripper to keep publishing position in a closed-loop.\n\nWe understand this is a limitation for teams for this phase of the competition which is due to the physical hardware but we will take this into account when evaluating teams submissions. Also during the physical deployment phase we will provide to the teams that qualify access to the physical TIAGo PRo robot for testing efore competition day\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/467877ff-5de4-4b2e-8c91-6fcaeb05a068",
