        "created_at":  "2026-09-05T10:23:57Z",
        "updated_at":  "2026-09-05T10:23:57Z",
        "body":  "@kdeesi \n\nThanks for the branch. We tried **8b5f261** but couldn\u0027t reproduce your result.\n\nCould you share the test world and the test_book SDF from your video? We\u0027re testing with the competition book in the arena world, so if test_book differs in size, mass or friction that would explain the difference.\n\nWhat we get with the competition book: free space test, book placed within 0.5 mm with the spine square across the jaws, 3 out of 3 fail. We also swept the close target across the band around the 2 cm spine, from 0.012 down to 0.002, and the joint lands exactly on its command every time, five decimal places, while /contacts logs around 5000 contact events with the book. So it\u0027s touching it, but loading the servo by zero.\n\nOn the closed loop idea, we measured the effort state and it doesn\u0027t seem to respond to load. Free air closed came out at mean 0.1553, closed on the book at mean 0.1551, same spread, and the on book max was actually lower. So we couldn\u0027t find a signal to close the loop on. Happy to be wrong here if we\u0027re reading the wrong topic or state interface, just point us at the one you\u0027d use and we\u0027ll test again.\n\nAlso a small thing: 8b5f261 has some broken mesh references. base_antenna_link_mirror.stl and wheel_link_reverted.stl don\u0027t exist, the files are named ...reflected.stl, so three visuals fail to load. Four suspension*_reflected references were also swapped to the non reflected mesh, so the mirrored links end up with wrong handed collision geometry.\n\nOne more question, will this go into main or a tagged release before the 15th? We can\u0027t really build against a branch that won\u0027t be in the released image.\n\nBR.",
        "author_association":  "NONE",
